# Code used for NOBSD conformal and mesh generation
This directory contains most of the code used in the following publication:

Ezendam, T., van der, Hofmeyer, H., van der Wal, S., Perevendieva K.G., and Emmerich, M. T. M. "Three new methods to automatically generate a finite element mesh for complex building representations in conceptual design simulation and optimization". In: (Submitted to ) (2025), 

The following code is included in this directory:

* an executable to test the IP and TP method on their capability of generating a conformal geometry
* an executable 
* an executable to compare the mesh quality of the IP and TP method with a benchmark case.

Furthermore the following supplementary data is supplied:

* the building spatial designs used for the each of the case studies
* the settings (structural and thermal design) used for the case studies
* data_files for 

## Reproducibility
Note that the code has been updated since the publication, and that some results may possibly not be reproduced with the latest version of the toolbox.
The studies in the publication have been carried out using vx of the toolbox.
In case the reader cannot reproduce the exact results, he/she is advised to contact an admin of the toolbox.

Besides these notions, the Data_files used to produce the graphs in directory "Mesh_quality_study_IP_TP_method" are added for reference as well as their resulting graphs. 